  "instructions": [
    "Bring 3 cups water and the rice to a boil in a medium pot. Cover, reduce to low, and cook 15 minutes until the water is absorbed. Keep covered off the heat.",
    "Cut the tofu into 3/4 inch cubes and pat dry. Toss gently with 2 tbsp of the cornstarch and the salt.",
    "Heat 3 tbsp oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the tofu in one layer and cook 8 minutes, turning, until golden and crisp on most sides. Move to a plate.",
    "Whisk the soy sauce, maple syrup, rice vinegar, 1/2 cup water, and the remaining 1 tbsp cornstarch in a small bowl.",
    "Add the remaining 1 tbsp oil to the skillet. Cook the broccoli, bell pepper, and carrots 4 minutes, stirring, until bright and just tender.",
    "Add the garlic and ginger and stir 30 seconds until fragrant.",
    "Stir the sauce and pour it into the skillet. Simmer 1 to 2 minutes until it thickens and coats the vegetables.",
    "Return the tofu to the skillet and toss gently to coat. Serve over the rice."
  ],
